WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:03.270
- [Narrator] This airfield
was once a strategic base

00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:05.610
for Russian forces in Kherson.

00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:08.280
Now, drone footage taken
after Moscow's retreat

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:09.150
in early November,

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:11.853
shows it littered with
destroyed military equipment.

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:15.840
Piles of damaged,
seemingly unusable hardware

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:17.670
sit on roads and fields,

00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:19.500
offering clues on Russia's strategy

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:21.093
for the next phase of the war.

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:24.930
After losing Kherson, Russia
launched missile attacks

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:27.180
on Kiev and other Ukrainian cities,

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:29.040
but along the front lines
in Southern Ukraine,

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:32.613
Moscow's focusing on reinforcing
its positions further east.

00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:35.820
So here's how images
from this liberated city,

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:37.830
help understand Russia's military shift

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:39.090
ahead of the winter,
(gunfire ringing)

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:41.913
when extremely cold weather
complicates operations.

00:00:42.870 --> 00:00:44.520
But first, let's look at this airfield,

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:48.330
which was used by Russian forces
as a base for its aviation.

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:51.480
These satellite images show
how Moscow housed helicopters,

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:53.580
trucks, and other military equipment here,

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:56.520
after occupying Kherson, in
the early days of the war.

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:59.100
The resources were meant to
support their Army's attacks,

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:01.680
and a push to conquer new territory.

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:04.320
However, they were also
exposed to Ukrainian attacks

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:06.390
that inflicted heavy damage on equipment,

00:01:06.390 --> 00:01:09.900
like these helicopters that
were hit as early as March.

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:10.950
And in recent months,

00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:13.440
analysts say, "Those positions
had become untenable,

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:15.390
as Ukraine also hit supply lines

00:01:15.390 --> 00:01:17.460
and infrastructure like this bridge,

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:20.100
making it difficult for
Russia to send ammunition,

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:23.250
and in the long-term,
support any attacks."

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:24.420
Russia's Defense Minister

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:26.790
announced the withdrawal from
the area on November 9th,

00:01:26.790 --> 00:01:28.170
saying, "The safety and well-being

00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:30.787
of military personnel was paramount."

00:01:30.787 --> 00:01:32.430
"But weeks before that announcement,

00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:34.500
Russia had already started
to withdraw its soldiers

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:36.840
as it also evacuates civilians,"

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:38.100
that's according to analysts,

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:39.457
and Kherson residents who say,

00:01:39.457 --> 00:01:42.600
"They noticed unusual
movements since October."

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:43.620
Troops took the time

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:45.660
to move equipment across
the Dnieper River,

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:48.690
towards territory Russia
controls in the East.

00:01:48.690 --> 00:01:50.550
The process appeared to be more organized

00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:52.710
than earlier Russian retreats.

00:01:52.710 --> 00:01:54.420
In the Kharkiv Region, for example,

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:56.310
Russian troops were
forced down in September,

00:01:56.310 --> 00:01:58.980
after a surprise counteract by Ukraine.

00:01:58.980 --> 00:02:01.980
Back then, the Ukrainian Army
took over tanks, howitzers,

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:04.350
and many other functioning weapons.

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:06.960
But in Kherson, the vast
majority of the gear left behind

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:08.460
appeared to be heavily damaged,

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:11.790
pointing to what analysts say,
"Is a pre-planned operation."

00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:13.500
Although Ukrainian propaganda videos

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:14.340
promoted the idea

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:17.010
that Russia had abandoned
valuable tanks and ammunition,

00:02:17.010 --> 00:02:20.047
defense analysts and WSJ
reporters in Kherson said,

00:02:20.047 --> 00:02:21.360
"The number of recovered weapons

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:23.280
appears to be minimal."

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:25.447
Weapons experts who
review these images say,

00:02:25.447 --> 00:02:27.540
"They believe some tanks
and armored vehicles

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:28.680
were intentionally destroyed

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:30.660
by Russian forces before they fled,

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:33.323
so they couldn't be
used by the Ukrainians."

00:02:33.323 --> 00:02:34.350
(crowd cheering)

00:02:34.350 --> 00:02:35.820
For Ukraine, taking back Kherson

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:38.010
was an important symbolic victory.

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:38.977
Military analysts say,

00:02:38.977 --> 00:02:40.710
"Moscow has paired some losses,

00:02:40.710 --> 00:02:41.760
and has the possibility

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:44.790
to reorganize and redeploy
to other fronts in the East,

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:46.980
where it has also
struggled to make gains."

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:48.337
For both armies, analysts say,

00:02:48.337 --> 00:02:50.460
"It's also a chance to
replenish their armories,

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:53.100
and stock up supplies
as temperatures fall,

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:55.775
and combat conditions
become more challenging.

00:02:55.775 --> 00:03:00.356
(tranquil music)
(wind gushing)

